From: MyOS cports <cports@myos.local>
Subject: [PATCH] avoid ambiguous negated string comparison

Perl 5.42 diagnoses "! $value eq ''" under warnings as a possible
precedence error.  texi2any's tests intentionally compare stderr with
reference output, so this warning makes the whole Perl converter test group
fail even though conversion succeeds.  Spell the intended non-empty string
test directly.

--- a/tp/Texinfo/Convert/Converter.pm
+++ b/tp/Texinfo/Convert/Converter.pm
@@ -386,7 +386,7 @@ sub output_internal {

   my $fh;
   my $encoded_output_file;
-  if (! $output_file eq '') {
+  if ($output_file ne '') {
     my $path_encoding;
     ($encoded_output_file, $path_encoding)
       = $self->encoded_output_file_name($output_file);
--- a/tp/Texinfo/Convert/LaTeX.pm
+++ b/tp/Texinfo/Convert/LaTeX.pm
@@ -1085,7 +1085,7 @@ sub convert {

   my $fh;
   my $encoded_output_file;
-  if (! $output_file eq '') {
+  if ($output_file ne '') {
     my $path_encoding;
     ($encoded_output_file, $path_encoding)
       = $self->encoded_output_file_name($output_file);
